<%- include('partials/header', {title: 'AWS Instance Scheduler — Serverless Automation'}) %>

<section class="project-hero">
  <a href="/" class="project-back-btn"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
  <h1>AWS Instance Scheduler (Serverless Automation)</h1>
  <p>Serverless solution to start/stop EC2 instances on schedule using Lambda, EventBridge, and DynamoDB. Deployed via CloudFormation and CircleCI.</p>
  <div class="project-hero-tags">
    <span>Lambda</span><span>EventBridge</span><span>DynamoDB</span><span>CloudFormation</span><span>CircleCI</span><span>Serverless</span>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="project-details">
  <div class="center">
    <img src="/images/aws-instance-scheduler.png" alt="AWS Instance Scheduler Architecture" class="project-diagram">
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
    <p>This project demonstrates <strong>serverless automation</strong> for managing EC2 instance lifecycles to reduce costs. The AWS Instance Scheduler framework automatically starts and stops EC2 instances based on schedules defined in DynamoDB.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Integrated <strong>GitHub and CircleCI</strong> for automated deployment (CI/CD).</li>
      <li>Deployed all infrastructure via <strong>CloudFormation</strong> as code.</li>
      <li>Used <strong>EventBridge cron</strong> and <strong>Lambda</strong> for time-based execution.</li>
      <li>Stored schedules in <strong>DynamoDB</strong> (e.g., "office-hours").</li>
      <li>Tagged EC2 instances with schedule names to control their runtime.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Architecture Explanation</h3>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🔄 CI/CD</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>GitHub</strong> — Source code storage</li>
          <li><strong>CircleCI</strong> — Automated deployment</li>
          <li><strong>CloudFormation</strong> — Infrastructure as Code</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>⚡ Scheduler Core</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EventBridge</strong> — Runs every 5 minutes</li>
          <li><strong>Lambda</strong> — Reads schedule, starts/stops EC2</li>
          <li><strong>DynamoDB</strong> — Stores schedule definitions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-component">
        <h4>🖥️ Targets</h4>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>EC2 Instances</strong> — Tagged with schedule name</li>
          <li><strong>IAM Role</strong> — Least-privilege for Lambda</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section">
    <h3>Key Learnings</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Deployed AWS Instance Scheduler using <strong>CloudFormation templates</strong>.</li>
      <li>Configured <strong>CircleCI environment variables</strong> securely for AWS deployment.</li>
      <li>Used serverless components (Lambda, DynamoDB, EventBridge) for cost automation.</li>
      <li>Understood how <strong>EC2 tagging and scheduling</strong> reduce runtime costs.</li>
      <li>Learned how CI/CD integrates with IaC for real-world automation.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="project-section alt-bg">
    <h3>Notes & Best Practices</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Use <strong>least-privilege IAM roles</strong> for Lambda and CloudFormation.</li>
      <li>Store AWS credentials securely using <strong>CircleCI environment variables</strong>.</li>
      <li>Define granular schedules for different environments (dev, test, prod).</li>
      <li>Review <strong>CloudWatch logs</strong> regularly for Lambda execution results.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="center">
    <a href="/" class="btn-back"><i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to Portfolio</a>
